 Add `--custom-speed` only when the user explicitly asks to customize Fast for this job. Add `--dry-run` only when the user asks for planning without execution. Use `--policy quality` only when maximum quality is explicitly preferred; otherwise keep `balanced`.
 
+Choose waiting value from the user's working context, without an extra model call. Pass `--wait-value background` for explicitly unattended, overnight, or non-blocking batch work. Use `--wait-value blocking` (the default) when the user is waiting on the result to continue. Do not equate a hidden background controller with a background user priority, or infer priority from model strength or task length. The planner can mark an individual non-blocking task `wait_value: "background"`; a background job cannot be promoted by a task hint.
+
+Fast selection first respects the saved matrix, then waiting value and comparable observed benefit. Explicit `all-fast` and `follow-entry` profiles retain their exact requested tiers. The benefit filter never adds model calls, upgrades a Standard cell, or changes an in-flight invocation. With missing or ambiguous evidence it preserves the profile. Use `--no-adaptive-fast` only when the user wants to disable benefit-based adjustments; the waiting-value rule still applies. Report the recorded selection reason instead of claiming an unmeasured saving.
+
+When the user supplies input materials, stage a second UTF-8 JSON file and pass `--materials-file <file>` to `start`, `run`, `steer`, or `followup`. Classify from the task and attachment metadata before reading attachment contents; do not make an extra model call. Use this shape, with the actual local paths and MIME types (MIME may be omitted when the extension is known):
+
+```json
+{"planning_reads_materials": true, "attachments": [{"path": "C:/input/report.pdf", "mime_type": "application/pdf"}]}
+```
+
+Set `planning_reads_materials=true` only when the existing planner needs to inspect those materials to formulate the plan, such as planning revisions from an attached manuscript. Use `false` when a general plan can be made without reading them, even if execution will later read files. With no such need, or no attachments, preserve the original speed selection. Count only user-supplied input materials: neither the task staging file, ordinary workspace files, nor outputs are attachments. Preserve the source paths in the task; remove the metadata staging file after the command copies it.
+
+For automatic profiles, more than five images (six or more), or any non-image attachment, selects Standard only for a planner that needs to read those materials. Both conditions must hold. The same existing planner and any validation retries are used; do not add a planning step. After planning, workers and reviews resume the saved matrix plus waiting-value and observed-benefit filters, rather than forcing Fast. Explicit `all-fast` and `follow-entry` retain precedence. `--no-adaptive-fast` does not disable the material rule. A replacement objective without a manifest clears the previous material condition; linked new jobs do not inherit old attachment metadata.
+
+This controls runner-owned calls after entry. It cannot change the already-started desktop entry request or switch a single invocation between input, reasoning, and output phases. Do not edit the global Codex service tier to implement this rule.
+
 The command returns immediately with `job_id`. If it returns `waiting_for_speed`, give the local setup link to the user. No model has been invoked yet. If the page is unavailable, render the status-provided text matrix, normalize the user's reply without guessing, echo the normalized matrix, and apply it through a UTF-8 text or JSON file.
 
